                                "example_id": "46fa113d-60b7-4536-8877-cb71a004f6d7",
                                "sense_id": "9a21aeb7-318c-361b-bd68-62c83d64033f",
                                "text": "A bendlet between two tirrets, over all a lion, rampant. […] On the Shield of dripstone^([sic]) of Door, a rose within a wreath; the tirrets are profusely used on the wooden ceiling and in the moulding, both external and internal. The wreath is also met with several times."
                            },
